1 OCCU Head of Kuhn, Loeb & Co., Head of Kuhn, Loeb & Co., bankers Zwischen 1890 und 1920 and 4 more occupations
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} birth names
2 CONT
2 CONT Jacob Hirsch Schiff 
2 CONT
2 CONT Jakob Heinrich Schiff 
2 CONT
2 CONT =========================================================================================
2 CONT
2 CONT "Jacob Henry Schiff (born Jakob Heinrich Schiff; January 10, 1847 – September 25, 1920) was an American banker, businessman, and philanthropist. He helped finance, among many other things, the Japanese military efforts against Tsa
2 CONC rist Russia in the Russo-Japanese War.
2 CONT
2 CONT Born in Frankfurt, Germany, Schiff migrated to the United States after the American civil war, and joined the firm Kuhn, Loeb & Co. From his base on Wall Street, he was the foremost Jewish leader from 1880 to 1920 in what later be
2 CONC came known as the "Schiff era", grappling with all major Jewish issues and problems of the day, including the plight of Russian Jews under the Tsar, American and international anti-semitism, care of needy Jewish immigrants, and th
2 CONC e rise of Zionism.He also became the director of many important corporations, including the National City Bank of New York, Equitable Life Assurance Society, Wells Fargo & Company, and the Union Pacific Railroad. In many of his in
2 CONC terests he was associated with E.H. Harriman."
2 CONT
2 CONT ======================================================================================
2 CONT
2 CONT Wikipedia links:
