1 NAME Jean Albert /Seligmann/
2 GIVN Jean Albert
2 SURN Seligmann
2 _MARNM Seligmann
1 SEX M
1 BURI
2 PLAC Nanterre, Hauts-de-Seine, France
2 ADDR
1 BIRT
2 DATE 15 JUN 1903
2 ADDR
3 CITY Paris 16e
3 STAE Île-de-France
3 CTRY France
1 DEAT
2 DATE 15 DEC 1941
2 PLAC Fort Mont-Valérien
2 ADDR
3 CITY Suresnes
3 STAE Île-de-France
3 CTRY France
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://fusilles-40-44.maitron.fr/?article145774
2 CONT
2 CONT Jean A. Seligmann was the son of the art dealer Arnold Seligmann (1870–1932), who had immigrated from Frankfurt. He separated from his brother Jacques Seligmann in 1912 and ran the art dealership “Arnold Seligmann & Cie.” in the f
2 CONC irst district of Paris at 23 Place Vendôme . After the death of his father in 1932, Jean A. Seligmann took over this ("Jean A. Seligman & Cie.").
2 CONT
2 CONT As announced by the Minister of Finance in May 1940 [1] , the gallery and its collections were confiscated by the "Forex Protection Command" in July 1940 and sold at a public auction. [2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Members of the German Wehrmacht arrested the art dealer on March 29, 1941 on suspicion of espionage on his frequent business trips in the pre-war period. He was imprisoned in the Cherche-Midi prison in Paris and shot on December 1
2 CONC 5, 1941 in the Mont-Valérien fortress as a hostage in retaliation for attacks by the French resistance . The German death certificate indicated the time of death for that day as “around 10:10 am”. [3]
2 CONT
2 CONT In view of the decree of January 16, 1941, the Secretary of State for Industrial Production, Pierre Pucheu, placed the company under provisional administration on the grounds that the management of A. Seligmann et Cie, antiquités 
2 CONC was unable to carry out its duties . [4] The government gazette of the French Republic reported in May 1942 that the art dealer Willy Remon had been appointed as provisional manager of the Seligmann Gallery. [5]
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1941, Paul Lindpaintner 's art dealership at the same address replaced the Berlin branch of Arnold Seligmann & Co., GmbH., Antiques, W 9, Bellevuestraße 5 [6] , which had been set up in 1932. [7] The Berlin art dealership of Jo
2 CONC hannes Hinrichsen was re-entered in the Berlin commercial register as a sole proprietorship at the changed address "Bellevuestraße 5" at his request on September 27, 1941. [ 8] From the received correspondence from May and April 1
2 CONC 941 it emerged that the art dealer Lindpaintner was in Paris at the time of the sale.
2 CONT
2 CONT Seligmann had been married to Henriette Marie, née Cretegny (* 1904), since 1938. The family lived with their two children at 24 Rue Barbet-de-Jouy in Paris. Producer Guy Seligmann (born March 24, 1939) is their son. 
