1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.deutsche-biographie.de/gnd136471404.html#ndbcontent
2 CONT
2 CONT https://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Harry_Fuld
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Translation:
2 CONT
2 CONT Harry Fuld (born February 3, 1879 in Frankfurt , † January 26, 1932 in Zurich ) was a German entrepreneur . He founded a company for the rental of house telephones , which became one of the leading companies in the telecommunicati
2 CONC ons industry in Europe. After the seizure of power by the NSDAP in early 1933, the Nazi regime expropriated Fuld's heirs because the family business was considered "Jewish".
2 CONT
2 CONT Life	 Edit
2 CONT
2 CONT Fuld was the only son of a wealthy Frankfurt art and antique dealer and was supposed to join the family-owned art and antique dealers J. and S. Goldschmidt . After completing a banking apprenticeship in Frankfurt and volunteering 
2 CONC in London , Paris and Brussels , there was no room for him in the family business. He then began to rent house phones based on the American model. After clarification of the legal situation, these facilities were admitted from 190
2 CONC 0 post office .
2 CONT
2 CONT Together with the German master watchmakers and technicians Carl Lehner (1871-1969) founded Fuld 1899 in Frankfurt, the German private telephone company H. Fuld & Co . This was converted 1928/1929 to the H. Fuld & CO. Telephone an
2 CONC d Telegraphenwerke AG and after Fulds death to the national telephone and Telegraphenwerke GmbH . After a boycott of the contract and the following " Aryanization " came out in 1937 the Telefonbau and standard time GmbH (T & N) . 
2 CONC The "normal time" refers to the production of electrical factory and station clocks .
2 CONT
2 CONT By 1925, a large part of the private telephone systems within and outside Germany were manufactured and maintained by his company. Fulds rapidly expanding operation had 1928 to a group with over 100 companies and an extensive bran
2 CONC ch network developed. Around 1930, Fulds Gesellschaft was one of the leading companies in the European telecommunications industry.
2 CONT
2 CONT Harry Fuld collected modern art and had, advised by the then director of the Frankfurt Städel Art Institute , Georg Swarzenski , built up an extensive collection whose fate is one of the more spectacular cases of robbery of recent
2 CONC  times. After Fulds death on a business trip to Switzerland in 1932, his sons Harry and Peter Harry Fuld and his widow had inherited the company and the art collection. While the company was already "Aryanized" in 1933, the author
2 CONC ities confiscated in 1941 the stored property of Fulds son Harry junior, who had emigrated in 1937 , including the image bought in 1917 by Harry Fuld senior Le Mur Rose ofHenri Matisse . It came into the possession of Kurt Gerstei
2 CONC ns in 1943 , was after his suicide in 1948 as "abandoned" and was only in 2008 restituted to the heirs Fulds . Peter Harry Fuld received after protracted negotiations his limited partnership in the company Telefonbau and normal ti
2 CONC me GmbH 1951 back.
