1 NAME Meyer (Meir ben Baruch Halevi Cassel) /Goldschmidt/
2 GIVN Meyer (Meir ben Baruch Halevi Cassel)
2 _MARNM Goldschmidt
2 NICK Meir ben Baruch Halevi
2 NICK Meir Kassel
2 NICK Meir Goldschmied-Kassel SeGaL
2 NICK Meyer Baruch (Benedikt) Cassel
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1621
2 PLAC Kassel
2 ADDR
3 STAE Hesse
3 CTRY Germany
1 DEAT
2 DATE 17 SEP 1667
2 PLAC Frankfurt am Main, Hessen-Nassau, Preussen
2 ADDR
1 BURI
2 DATE 18 SEP 1667
2 PLAC Battonnstraße Jewish cemetery, Frankfurt am Main, Hessen-Nassau, Preussen
2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Meyer is first mentioned in 1627 with his father Benedict and mother Rosina, when he was only six years old (StA Marburg, Best. 17 I Nr. 3726). Thus he was born ca. 1621. In 1620, his father Benedikt Goldschmidt wa
2 CONC s already living in Kassel. He is number nine on a list of ten tax-paying Jews, Benedikt paying the largest sum (Hallo 1930). Thus, Meyer was born in Kassel. He was given right of residence in Frankfurt am Main on December 27, 163
2 CONC 4, when he married (Dietz 1988: 149). His Yiddish family name Kassel proves that he is to be identified with the son of Benedict and Rosina. His tombstone calls him a parnas and mentions his Yiddish name, Meir Kassel (מאיר קאסל), 
2 CONC as well as his Hebrew name, Meir ben Baruch ha-Levi (מאיר בן ברוך הלוי). He was married to Bella (בילה אשת מאיר קאסיל), the daughter of Asher Anshel Segal Buchsbaum (בת אשר אנשיל סג"ל ב"ב).
2 CONT
2 CONT References:  Alexander Dietz, The Jewish Community of Frankfurt: A Genealogical Study 1349-1849 (Camelford, UK: Vanderher Publications, 1988). Rudolf Hallo, “Aus der Geschichte der Kasseler Gemeinde”, Jüdische Wochenzeitung für Ca
2 CONC ssel, Hessen und Waldeck 7 (1930), No. 48.
2 CONT
2 CONT For his descendants, see http://goldschmidt.tripod.com/golds1.htm.
