1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Ida Frankau was born 5 August 1847 in Whitechapel, Middlesex, England (now part of London) to Joseph Frankau and Emilie (Amelia) Geiger.[1][2] Her father was working in London as an importer of leeches at the time.
2 CONC [3] The birth was also registered in Germany.[4][5] In 1851 the family (Ida's parents, older sister Delia and younger brother Authur), lived in Islington in a household that included Ida's uncle and three servants.[3][6][7]
2 CONT
2 CONT A son was born to the couple on 4 April 1871 in Frankfurt am Main, Hessen-Nassau, Preußen, Deutschland.[8] He died the same day.[9]
2 CONT
2 CONT A daughter, Amalie Roeder, was born on 6 August 1872 in Frankfurt am Main, Hessen-Nassau, Preußen, Deutschland.[10][11]
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughter Anna Regina was born on 2 August 1875 in Frankfurt am Main, Hessen-Nassau, Preußen, Deutschland.[12][13][14]
2 CONT
2 CONT Anna, who married Leo Löwenherz and immigrated to the United States, travelled to Germany in 1920 to visit her ailing mother.[15][16]
2 CONT
2 CONT Anna died 13 May 1924.[6]
2 CONT Ida Frankau was born 5 August 1847 in Whitechapel, Middlesex, England (now part of London) to Joseph Frankau and Emilie (Amelia) Geiger. Her father was working in London as an importer of leeches at the time. The birth was also re
