1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Wilma Shannon Warburg, a civic leader and philanthropist, died on Friday at her home in Middleburg, Va. She was 89.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Warburg was a benefactor and board member of charitable organizations in Middleburg and New York City. She lived in Manhattan for many years.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was on the board of the Henry Street Settlement for nearly 30 years and was also an active supporter of Lenox Hill Hospital.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was married to Frederick Warburg, an investment banker, sportsman and philanthropist. He was the eldest son of Felix M. Warburg, a young German banker who became a major financier in the United States, whose family mansion on 
2 CONC Fifth Avenue is now the Jewish Museum.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Warburg was born in Rochester and graduated from Smith College.
2 CONT
2 CONT She worked in volunteer efforts during World War II, and after the war worked in management at Macy's.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her husband died in 1973. She is survived by nieces and nephews.
