1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://rudolfsonneborn.blogspot.com/
2 CONT
2 CONT Commissioned in the fledgling Naval Air Corp. in 1918 (WWI).  Trained as an aviator, but the war ended before the training ended.  
2 CONT Chairman of the Board of Sonneborn Chemical and Refining Co.
2 CONT
2 CONT From Bacharach Kestrich Family Tree: 
2 CONT Notes for RUDOLF GOLDSCHMID SONNEBORN: 
2 CONT Head of the "Sonneborn Institute" which gathered surreptitiously supplies, munitions and ships for liberation of Palestine (Israel). He was personally contacted by David Ben-Gurion who met with him and the other men at Sonneborn's
2 CONC  apartment in NYC on July 18, 1945. The most famous ship was the EXODUS. 
2 CONT Family: S. Siegmund B. and Camille K. (Goldschmid) S.; m. 2d. Dorothy Schiff, 1953. 
2 CONT Education: student, Park Sch., Johns Hopkins U., 1918; postgrad.,Harvard Bus. Sch., 1919-20. 
2 CONT Memberships: Nat. Petroleum Assn. (trustee), Pa. Grade Crude Oil Assn. (dir.), Am. Petroleum Inst. (past dir.), Advertising Club, Johns Hopkins Club, Pinnacle Club, Oil City Club, Twenty-Five Yrs. of Petroleum industry, Harvard Bu
2 CONC s. Sch. Club, Young Men's Philanthropic League. 
2 CONT Addresses: Home, New York, NY. Positions Held: pres., Sonneborn Chem. and Refining Co. (became part of Witco Chem. Co. Inc., 1960), until 1960; dir., sec., treas., Sonneborn Chem. and Refining Co. (became part of Witco Chem. Co. I
2 CONC nc., 1960). Career-Related: pres., dir. Petroleum Transport & Trading Corp., Sonneborn Assocs. Petroleum Corp., N.Y. Post Corp., Sonapco Bank St. Corp. Alliance Indsl. Devel. Corp., Alliance Industries Inc., Pan Alliance Corp., De
2 CONC l Amkor Corp., Ampak-Am.Israel Corp., Israel Devel. Corp., Israel Am. Indsl Devel. Bank Ltd., Palestine Econ. Corp., Am. Israeli Fin. Corp.; chmn. bd. Am. Palestine Trading Corp.; pres. Israel Am. Petroleum Corp.; founder Material
2 CONC  for Israel; dir. Am. Com. for Weizmann Inst. Sci., Am. Friends of Hebrew U., Coun. Jewish Fedns. & Welfare Funds; treas., dir. Breth Found., Bezalel Found.; dir. Hirschman Found., Post Found; nat. chmn. United Jewish Appeal, 1950
2 CONC -44; hon. co-chmn. United Jewish Appeal Greater N.Y.; past pres. Oil Trades Assn. Inc., N.Y.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lived in the Regency Hotel 525 E 86th St in the 60s-70s.  Also had a country home, Twin Hills, in Danbury, CT.
2 CONT
2 CONT "California, County Marriages, 1850-1953", database with images, FamilySearch (https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:K864-8S4 : 18 August 2022), Rudolf Goldschmid Sonneborn and Dorothy Schiff, 1953.
2 CONT
2 CONT ____
2 CONT
2 CONT Sereral "sources" erroneously give his birthdate as June 20.  It was the 22nd.  He celebrated annually witj a big elegant dinner party at The Regency Hotel, where he lived. with all the family (ages 13 and up, though that was rela
2 CONC xed in later years), distant cousins , and close friends.  These parties are the reason so many cousins have met and maintained contact.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT --------
2 CONT License TO MARRY  Dorothy Schiff was ISSUED on 8/18/1953.  The marriage may have taken place several days or weeks later.  Ignore the conflicting data.  
2 CONT
2 CONT ______________
2 CONT
2 CONT Awarded a[n Honorary ?] Doctorate in Humane Letters from Hebrew Union College in 1973.
