1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Louis Schwarzschild was born in 1841 in Franfurt, Germany. He moved to France as a boy, and at age 15 worked in a cloth factory and later worked as a salesman for a hop and wine establishment. He came to California
2 CONC  in 1861 and entered the toy business, employed by Thurnauer and Finn, and was considered one of the best judges of toys in the county. He made annual trips to Europe as a purchaser. In 1860 he co partnered the firm of Feinburg an
2 CONC d Schwarzschild at 520 - 526 Market Street in San Francisco, employing 41 people in various departments. The firm was the only toy establishment on the Pacific Coast and did an annual business of about $500,000. He was married in 
2 CONC San Francisco in 1867 to Amelia Ochs, also a native of Frankfort on Main.They had five daughters - Alice (Mrs M.S. Hellman of Los Angeles), Leontine, Adele, Jennie (Mrs. Gus Harris of Spokane, Wa) and Flora
2 CONT
2 CONT The Bay of San Francisco: The Metropolis of the Pacific Coast and ..., Volume 2 = page 14, published 1892 
