2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Max Baer and his wife Karoline (nee Strauss) owned from 1861 to 1880 the magnificent "Gasthaus sum Straussen on the City Hall Square of Mergentheim.  It dates from about 1400.  The present structure was erected in 1577.  The first
2 CONC  mention of the name "sum Straussen" appears in the archive documents of 1620.  The Strausses were wine merchants.  [This information comes from Hank Stroud around 1974. He is a descendent of Nathan (ben Samuel) Strauss of Dittigh
2 CONC eim.]  
2 CONT
2 CONT Note that Mergentheim is the same town that Leopold Strauss (1859-1922) came from!
